          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_batch_a_a_results" kindref="compound">BatchAAResults</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>AA</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Given a memory Mod/Ref/ModRef&apos;ing instruction, calling this will give you the nearest dominating <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_access" kindref="compound">MemoryAccess</ref> that Mod&apos;s the location the instruction accesses (by skipping any def which <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_a_a" kindref="compound">AA</ref> can prove does not alias the location(s) accessed by the instruction given). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Note that this will return a single access, and it must dominate the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_instruction" kindref="compound">Instruction</ref>, so if an operand of a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_phi" kindref="compound">MemoryPhi</ref> node Mod&apos;s the instruction, this will return the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_phi" kindref="compound">MemoryPhi</ref>, not the operand. This means that given: if (a) { 1 = MemoryDef(liveOnEntry) store a } else { 2 = MemoryDef(liveOnEntry) store b } 3 = MemoryPhi(2, 1) MemoryUse(3) load a</para>
<para>calling this API on load(a) will return the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_phi" kindref="compound">MemoryPhi</ref>, not the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_memory_def" kindref="compound">MemoryDef</ref> in the if (a) branch. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
